    <!-- ===== Quick help ===== -->

    <string name="help_title">Quick help</string>
    <string name="help_detecting_title">Detecting a chord</string>
    <string name="help_detecting_body">Press Detect Chord and strum. It listens until the answer settles — usually well under a second — and strumming again restarts it, so a bad take needs no second press. Hold the phone near the guitar; a quiet unplugged instrument across the room is hard work.</string>
    <string name="help_wrong_chord_title">If it picks the wrong chord</string>
    <string name="help_wrong_chord_body">The best fit is a guess, not gospel. Tap anything in the \"Or did you mean\" row to see that chord instead.</string>
    <string name="help_capo_title">Using a capo</string>
    <string name="help_capo_body">Press Set Capo, under the Detect Chord button. It does not change detection — the microphone hears the real chord either way — but it changes the shapes you are shown so they match your hands, and fret numbers are the ones printed on your neck.</string>
    <string name="help_vocabulary_title">What it knows</string>
    <string name="help_vocabulary_body">Major, minor, 7, maj7, m7, sus2 and sus4, in standard tuning. Richer chords (6ths, 9ths, altered dominants) are out of scope and will come back as the nearest chord it does know.</string>

